libvmdk is a library to access the VMware Virtual Disk (VMDK) format.

Project information:

* Status: alpha
* Licence: LGPL-3.0-or-later

Read supported extent file formats:

* RAW (flat)
* COWD version 1 (sparse)
* VMDK version 1, 2 and 3 (sparse)

Supported VMDK format features:

* delta links
* automatic snapshot chain discovery through parentCID and parentFileNameHint
* reading a snapshot chain at a descriptor or Unix timestamp
* grain compression (as of version 20131209)
* data markers (as of version 20140416)

Snapshot chains:

* `libvmdk_handle_open_snapshot_chain()` opens a snapshot and all of its parents
* `libvmdk_handle_open_snapshot_chain_at_index()` opens an older point in the chain
* `libvmdk_handle_open_snapshot_chain_at_timestamp()` selects the newest snapshot
  whose descriptor modification time is at or before the supplied Unix timestamp
* snapshot index 0 is the oldest (base) image; the last index is the active image
* both sparse and stream optimized extents are supported, including parent fallback

The `vmdkinfo -s` option lists the snapshot chain. Use `vmdkinfo -t <timestamp>`
to inspect the snapshot selected at a historical Unix timestamp.

VMDK format features not supported at the moment:

* images that use a physical device
* changed block tracking (CBT) (supported by VMDK version 3 (sparse)) / change tracking file

Work in progress:

* Dokan library support
* Thread-safety in handle API functions

For more information see:

* Project documentation: https://github.com/libyal/libvmdk/wiki/Home
* How to build from source: https://github.com/libyal/libvmdk/wiki/Building

